hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9241","Mahmoud ibn Ghaylan informed us, he said: An-Nadr ibn Shumail informed us, he said: Shu`bah informed us, he said: Khalifa informed us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr said: Do not wear your wives with silk, for I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.”"
"9242","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Raja told us, he said: Harb told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Imran bin Hattan told me that he asked Abdullah bin Abbas about wearing silk, and he said: Ask Aisha, so I asked Aisha, and she said: Ask Abdullah bin Omar, so I asked Ibn Omar, and he said: Abu Hafs told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears silk in This world, he will have no share in the Hereafter.”"
"9243","Suleiman bin Salam told us, he said: Al-Nadr informed us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, and Bishr Ibn Al-Muhtafiz, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Only someone who has no manners wears silk.”"
"9244","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abu Nu’man told us, in the year two hundred and seven, he said: Al-Sa’q bin Hazan told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Ali Al-Bariqi, he said: A woman came to me asking me a question, and I said to her: This is Ibn Umar, so she followed him asking him, and I followed her, hearing what He says, She said: Give me a fatwa about silk. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it.”"
"9245","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Omar, he said: “Beware of wearing silk clothing, for The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade wearing silk clothing except for this, and he raised his index and middle fingers.”"
"9246","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, he said: We were with Utba bin Yazid, Then Omar’s letter came, stating that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one should wear silk, except one who has nothing of it in the Hereafter, except like this.” Abu Uthman said with his two fingers that surrounded the thumb: I saw them as the buttons of the tyalisa, until I saw the tyalisa."
"9247","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Abu Uthman, he said: The letter of Omar came to us, While we are in Azerbaijan, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade silk, except for this: two fingers. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9248","Amr bin Ali told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Omar, he said: “A Prophet forbade me.” God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, abstained from wearing silk, except for the place of two fingers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9249","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Amir al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghaflah, Omar addressed the collector, and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade wearing silk, except where two or three fingers are located. \or four\"""""""
"9250","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, that Omar, he said: “No “You shall wear silk except for such and such.” Yazid said: I do not know how he said it"
"9251","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: I am Al-Fadl, meaning Ibn Musa, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, he said: Omar said: “Put on pieces of silk this way and that way: two fingers, or three, or four.”"
"9252","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Wabarah, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, he said: Omar said: “It is not permissible, or not appropriate, to be made of silk except like this and like this: two fingers wide, or three, or four in circumference or buttoned.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9253","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Wabara, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla. H And Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Suwayd bin He neglected, according to Omar, “that he did not mark in the brocade except the place of four fingers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9254","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Isa bin Yunus, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He delivered a license to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam in a silk shirt from Mecca, which they had with them when they were travelling."
"9255","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, “that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He handed over a piece of clothing to Abd al-Rahman, while al-Zubayr was wearing a silk shirt because of an itch they had.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9256","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham bin Othman Al-Basri told me, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that Abd al-Rahman bin Awf and al-Zubayr complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about lice, so he granted them permission to wear a silk shirt. Anas said: I saw a silk shirt on them."
"9257","Ammar bin Al-Hasan Al-Razi told us, saying: Abu Abdul Rahman Abdullah bin Saad, also called Al-Dashtaki, told me on the authority of his father, saying: I saw a man wearing a black turban, and he was wearing a black turban. He was placing his hand on it and saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, clothed it.”"
"9258","Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Peace be upon him, wearing a red robe, walking. I have never seen before him or after him anyone more beautiful than him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9259","Hannad bin Al-Sirri informed us, on the authority of Abtar, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Siwar Kufi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: “I saw The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was wearing a red robe one night, so I started looking at him and the moon, for it is more beautiful to me than the moon.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is wrong and the one before it is correct, 5 and Ash’ath is weak 5 (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9260","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhaifah, on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He came out in a red robe and set aside a goat to pray to, behind which the dog, the woman, and the donkey passed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9261","Abu Al-Ash’ath Ahmad ibn Al-Miqdam Al-Ijli told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Zuray’, he said: Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Wear white clothes. And shroud your dead in it, for it is better and purer.”"
"9262","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Aliyah, and Ubayd Allah bin Amr Al-Raqqi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, On the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You must wear white clothes for your living to wear, and shroud yourself.” In it are your dead, for it is among the best of your garments.”"
"9263","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Samurah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “You must wear white clothes, so that your living may wear them, and shroud your dead in them, for they are among the best of your clothes.”"
"9264","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: I heard Saeed bin Abi Arouba, narrating on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abi Qalaba On the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Put on white clothes, for they are purer. And the best, and shroud your dead in it.” Yahya said: I did not write it. I said: Why? He said: I have dispensed with the hadith of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Samurah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9265","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “He loved The clothes are for the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9266","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid, who is Ibn Al-Harith, told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, On the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, that Khalid bin Ma’dan informed him, that Jubayr bin Nufayr informed him, that Abdullah bin Amr informed him The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him wearing two saffron clothes, and he said: “These are the clothes of infidels, so do not wear them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9267","Hajib bin Sulaiman al-Munbiji told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Amr said that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing a saffron garment. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry and said: “Go.” So cast them away from you.” He said: Where are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “In the fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9268","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn told him That his father told him that he heard Ali say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing a gold ring and wearing a bow’s garment. And the rainforest, and the recitation of the Qur’an, while I was bowing.”"
"9269","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told me, he said: Al-Qanabi told us, he said: Ishaq bin Abi Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Hunayn, that his father He told him that Ali bin Abi Talib said: “My beloved forbade me from wearing cloth and turban, and from wearing rings with gold, and from wearing I recite while bowing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9270","Ibrahim bin Harun Al-Balkhi told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Abdullah Ibn Hunayn, on the authority of Ali, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me, and I do not say He forbade you from wearing gold seals, from reciting the Qur’an while bowing, and from wearing a bow, and added a fourth to it: “And from the yellow one that is presented.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9271","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of some of Abbas’s loyalists, On the authority of Ali, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade the wearing of dyed hair and harsh clothes, and the reading of the Qur’an while bowing.” \"" 9272"""""
"9272","Ahmad ibn Sa'id informed me, saying: 'Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, that 'Ali said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade me from wearing saffron-dyed garments (mu'asfarah)."""""
"9273","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham told me, on the authority of Uthman, he said: Abu Amer told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah. Ibn Hunayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me about three things: from stamping gold, and from wearing Al-Mu’saffar, and about recitation while bowing.”"
"9274","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ismail, he said: Sharek told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of Ali, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me.” May God bless him and grant him peace, about stamping gold, about wearing saffron, and about reciting while bowing."
"9275","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Layth, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Khaled bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed. Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abdullah Ibn Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Aisha, that she told him that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He used to send his clothes: his shirt, his robe, and his lower garment to some of his family. \With saffron\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9276","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abu Nuh Abd al-Rahman bin Ghazwan told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Iyad bin Luqit, on the authority of Abu Rimthah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us, wearing two green garments.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9277","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Qais told us, on the authority of Khabbab bin Al-Art, He said: “We complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was leaning against his cloak in the shade of the Kaaba, so we said: Will you not ask for help for us? Do you pray to God for us? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9278","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ya’qub, who is Ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri, told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: A woman came with a garment, and Sahl said: Do you know what a garment is? They said: Yes, this shamla has its hem woven. She said: O Messenger of God, I wove this with my own hands and clothed it. So he took it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in need of it, so he came out to us, and it was his garment. Then a man from the people came and said: O Messenger of God, Cover it. He said: “Yes.” So he sat as long as God wished in the gathering, then he came back and folded it, then sent it to him, and the people said to him: What? You did well. You asked her, knowing that he does not refuse a question. The man said: By God, I only asked her so that it would be enough for me on the day I die. Sahl: it was his shroud"
"9279","Abu Bakr bin Ali Al-Maruzi told me, he said: Shayban told us, he said: Al-Saqq bin Hazan told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Hakam Al-Bunani told us, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: Safwan bin Assal told me, he said: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace peace be upon him while he was in the mosque, leaning on his cloak.”"
"9280","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Affan told me, he said: Hammam told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Aisha, “She made The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a black cloak. He remembered its blackness and its whiteness, so he put it on. When he sweated and smelled the scent of wool, he tossed it and was He loves the pleasant smell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9281","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, wrapped himself in a black cloak, making its black resemble its white, and making its white resemble its black, so he sweated and smelled the scent of wool. So he threw it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9282","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, he said: The Messenger of God swore May God bless him and grant him peace. He did not give Makhramah anything, so Makhramah said: O my son, go with us to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I went off with him, and he said: “Come in and call him for me.” He said: So I called him, and he came out to him wearing a cloak of it, and he said: “I have hidden this for you.” He said: Then he looked at it and said: “Radi Makhramah.”"
"9283","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, he said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he said: “O Mughirah, take the medicine.” So I took it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set off. He greeted him until he disappeared from me, and he relieved himself, and he was wearing a Syrian robe made of wool. So he went to take his hand out of its sleeve, and it narrowed, so he came out. He touched his hand from below, so I poured water on him, and he performed ablution as he did for prayer, and wiped over his socks, then prayed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9284","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ya’la told us, he said: Abd al-Malik told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: When Abdullah bin Ubayy died Ibn Salul, his son came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, if you do not bring it to him, he will continue to be taunted about it, so he brought it to him. They found him and had taken him into his pit. He said: “Before you enter him.” Then he was taken out of his pit and spit on him from his horn to his feet. And he put his shirt on him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9285","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Badil bin Maysarah, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, On the authority of Asmaa, she said: “The hand of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was up to the wrist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9286","Suleiman bin Salam informed us. He said: I am al-Nadr. He said: I am Musa bin Sarwan. He said: Badil al-Uqaili told me. He said: How many of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God grant him peace to the wrist.”"
"9287","Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Abdul-Mu’min bin Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Umm Salama She said: “The most beloved garment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the shirt.”"
"9288","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah informed us, saying: Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih On the authority of Abu Hurairah, “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, put on a shirt, he would start with his right hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9289","On the authority of Suleiman bin Salam, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Shammil, on the authority of Kahms, on the authority of Sayyar Al-Fazariyyah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Bhisa Al-Fazariyeh, on the authority of her father She said: “The father of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked permission, so he came between him and his shirt, so he began to kiss and cling to it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9290","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qais, he said: I brought, and Makhrifah Al-Abdi, with clothes from Hijr, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us while we were in Mina, and a weigher weighed for a fee, so he bought trousers from us, and he said For the weigher: “Weigh and swing.”"
"9291","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Samak, he said: I heard Abu Safwan, saying: “I sold from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought a man’s trousers before the Hijra for three dirhams, and he weighed for me, so he gave it to me.”"
"9292","Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashhar informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Malik Abu Safwan bin Amira said: “I sold a man’s trousers to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before the Hijra, and he gave me something.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9293","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Sahl bin Hammad Abu Attab Al-Dallal told me, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Samak bin Harb told us, He said: I heard Malik Abu Safwan say: “I came to Mecca and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was there, and a man bought a pair of trousers from me, and he weighed \So he preferred\"""""""
"9294","Muhammad bin Bashar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, talking about Arafat, so he said: “Whoever cannot find a garment should wear trousers, and whoever cannot find sandals should wear trousers.” Let him wear socks.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9295","Amr bin Mansour told me, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever cannot find a garment, let him wear trousers, and whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear socks.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9296","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Salim told him, Abdullah bin Omar told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Among us was a man dragging his garment out of arrogance. It will roll on the earth until the Day of Resurrection.”"
"9297","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’. H And Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever drags his garment, or says: The one who drags his garment, is out of arrogance, God will not look at him on the Day of \resurrection\"""""""
"9298","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muharib, he said: I heard Ibn Umar talking, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drags his garment out of imagination, God Almighty will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9299","Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Qurashi told me, he said: We were with Ali bin Al-Madini. He said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: We told him. My father, he said: I heard Jarir, who is Ibn Zaid, say: I was sitting with Salim bin Abdullah at the door of his house, when he passed by a young man from the Quraysh dragging He took off his garment, then he shouted at him and said: “Lift your garment,” and he began to apologize to him for making it so relaxed. Then Ali approached and said: “Abu Hurairah told us.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Among us was a man from among those who came before you, walking in a robe of his own that his soul admired, when he lost God blesses the earth, and he will dwell therein until the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9300","Al-Hasan bin Mudrak informed us, he said: Yahya, who is Ibn Hammad, told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, he said: He informed me Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever drags his garment out of vanity will not “It is permissible from God and not forbidden.”"
"9301","Ali bin Shuaib told us, he said: Abu Damra told us, reading, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Yahya Al-Aslami told me, on the authority of Ikrimah Mawla Ibn Abbas, that when Ibn Abbas put on his garment, he would loosen the front of his garment, so that his hem would fall on the back of his foot, and he would raise the garment from what behind him, so I said to him: Why are you wearing this? He said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing this garment.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9302","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath bin Sulaym, he said: I heard my aunt speaking, on the authority of Her uncle, he was in the city and saw a man saying: “Raise your garment, for he is more pious and more persistent.” So I looked, and it was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So I said: It is a salt cloak. He said: “Do you not have an example in me?” I looked, and lo, his lower garment reached half the shin. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9303","Amr ibn Yazid told us, he said: Bahz ibn Asad told us, 5 Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He is trustworthy 5, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Ash'ath ibn Sulaym said: I heard my aunt, speaking on the authority of her uncle, that he was walking in the city and saw a man. He said: \Raise your garment. For he is more persistent and more pious.” Then I looked and saw the Messenger of God"
"9304","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took hold of the muscle of my leg and said, “Girdle yourselves here,” lowering his muscle, “And if you refuse, then you have no right.” For the loincloth on the ankles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9305","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjumani Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Shuaib, who is Ibn Safwan, told us. On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took hold of the muscle of my leg and said: “This is the place If you refuse, then without this, and if you refuse, then the izaar has no right to the ankles.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Both hadiths are wrong, and the correct one is the one that follows them."
"9306","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim bin Yazid, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: He took The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, touched the lower part of my calf muscle, or his shin, and said: “This is the place of the garment. If you refuse, then lower. “I disagree, the lower garment on the ankles has no right.”"
"9307","Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Muhammad bin Qudamah informed us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim bin Yazid, on the authority of Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The place of the garment is up to the middle of the legs and the musculature. If you refuse, then lower. \I refuse. It is the middle of the leg"
"9308","Muhammad bin Adam Al-Masisi told me, he said: Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim bin Yazid, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his hand on the muscle of his leg, or my shin, then said: “This “The place of the garment.” Then he lowered his hand and said: “Then to here.” Then he lowered it again and said: “Otherwise, then to here.” Then he said: “ And the lower garment has no right to the ankles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9309","Ahmad bin Sulaiman informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Ubaid al-Tanafisi Kufi and Uthman bin Abdul Rahman al-Harrani told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim bin Yazid, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took hold of the muscle of my leg and said: “ The garment is here. If you refuse, then lower than that. If you refuse, then the ankles have no right to the garment.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9310","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ubaida al-Hujaimi, on the authority of Jabir bin Salim Al-Hujaimi said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was covering himself with a cloak of his, the fringe of which had been scattered over his foot, and I said: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: “Fear God, and do not despise anything that is good, even if you empty your bucket into the vessel for someone to draw water, even if You should speak to your brother with your face turned towards him, and beware of letting the garment fall apart, for letting the garment fall apart is a matter of imagination, and God does not like Imagination"
"9311","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Hammad bin Masada al-Basri told us, he said: Qurrah bin Khalid al-Basri told us, on the authority of Qurrah bin Musa Al-Hajimi. H Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Amir told us, he said: Qurrah bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Qurrah bin Musa al-Hujaimi, on the authority of Sulaym bin Jaber Al-Hujaimi said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was covering himself with a cloak, and its fringe was on his feet. I said: O Messenger God, advise me. He said: “You must fear God, and do not despise anything that is good, even if you speak to your brother with your face turned toward him. And beware of letting the garment slip, for it is only a matter of imagination, and God does not like it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9312","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Qurrah bin Khalid told us, he said: Qurrah bin Musa Al-Hujaimi told us, he said: Our sheikhs told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Jabir, who said: I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was covering himself in a cloak, even if his hem was On his feet, I said: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: “You must fear God, and do not despise anything that is good, even if you are just doing it.” For the one who is praying for rain, and beware of letting the garment slip, for it is a matter of imagination and God does not like it.”"
"9313","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim Al-Awdi told us, he said: Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Al-Hassan told us, he said: I heard an arrow. Ibn Al-Mu'tamir narrates, on the authority of Al-Hujaimi, that he came to Medina and met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in some of the alleys of Medina, and he agreed with him. Then he was garbed with a Qatari garment, his entourage scattered, and he said: “Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God.” Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ Peace be upon you. The greeting of the dead. He said: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: Do not despise any kind of kindness that you do, even if you donate it. Connecting the rope, even if you empty your bucket into the watering can, even if you meet your Muslim brother with your face extended toward him, even if You can keep the two beasts company with your own soul, even if you give the vastness.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sahm bin al-Mu’tamir is not known. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9314","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Abu Tamimah, and his name is Tarif bin Mujalid al-Basri, On the authority of a man from Bilhajim, he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I said: Advise me. He said: Do not insult anyone, and do not renounce Kindness, even if you speak to your brother while you are facing him with your face down, even if you empty your bucket into the watering can, and wear your girdle halfway. The leg, and if you refuse, then to the ankles, and beware of letting the garment slip, for letting the garment slip is a matter of imagination, and God does not like imagination.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9315","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham Al-Mughirah bin Salamah Al-Makhzoumi told us, he said: 5 Abu Abdul Rahman : And he is trustworthy 5, he said: Salam bin Miskin told us, he said: Aqeel bin Talha Al-Sulami told us, on the authority of Abu Juzy Al-Hujaimi, that he, he said: O Messenger By God, we are a people of the desert, so we would like you to teach us something that God may benefit us with. He said: “Do not despise anything that is recognised, even if Empty your bucket into the watering can, and even if you speak to your brother with your face turned toward him, and beware of unraveling the garment, for it is from Pride, and God does not like arrogance. If a man insults you for what he knows about you, do not insult him for what you know about him, for that will be a reward. That is for you, but his curse will be upon him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9316","Musa bin Abdul Rahman Al-Masruqi told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God does not look to a path.”"
"9317","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Adam bin Abi Iyas Al-Asqalani told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Saeed bin Jubayr told us, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God does not look to a path.”"
"9318","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Aqeel told us, he said: My grandfather told me, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: I heard Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God Almighty does not look to a path.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9319","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah, who is the son of Musa, told us, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “God does not look to the right path.”"
"9320","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ibn Mudarrak, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Kharshah bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three to whom God will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look.” to them, but He will not purify them, and for them is a painful punishment.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it, and Abu Dharr said: They were disappointed and lost. He said: “ “The one who gives is his garment, the one who spends is his goods with false oaths, and the one who is generous is his gift.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9321","Bishr bin Khalid told us, he said: Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Sulayman bin Mihran, who is Al-A’mash, on the authority of Sulayman bin Mushahir, on the authority of Kharshah ibn al-Hurr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three to whom God Almighty will not speak on the day of Resurrection, but He will not purify them, and for them will be a painful punishment. He who is generous with what he gives, and the one who sends is his burden, and the one who spends his goods by false oaths.”"
"9322","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that Ata Ibn Yasar told them, he said: A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not “The prayer of a man who has his garment draped will be accepted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9323","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am a partner, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Al-Husayn bin Qabisa, On the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taking the custody of Sufyan bin Sahl Al-Thaqafi, and he was saying: “Oh Sufyan bin Sahl, do not let your garment be let down, for God does not like those who let down.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9324","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Sa’id al-Maqbari told me, and he used to tell On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whatever is lower than the ankles of the garment is in Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9325","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid, who is Ibn Al-Harith, told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim said: Ibn Ya’qub told me that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whatever is under the ankles is The upper garment is in the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9326","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Isbaal in the garment, the shirt, and the turban. Whoever drags any of them out of arrogance, God will not look at him.” on the Day of Resurrection\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9327","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Musa bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever drags his garment out of vanity, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, one The two parts of my garment are relaxed, unless I promise to do so from him. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You are not one of those who do that out of arrogance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9328","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abu Amr, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer’s loincloth extends to the muscle of his leg, then to half of his leg, then to his ankle and below.” The two ankles of the garment are in the Fire.” Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Abu Al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus bin Al-Hajjaj, he said: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Muhammad narrated to us Ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Muslim’s loincloth,” and the hadith narrated (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9329","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Jacob, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whatever is under the ankles of the garment will be in the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9330","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yaqoub, the client of al-Harqa, he said: he said: Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer’s loincloth extends to the middle of his shins, and from below to above.” the ankles, and anything lower than that is in the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9331","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Mu’afa bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Fulayh bin Sulaiman Al-Madini told us, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer’s loincloth extends to the middle of his shins.” And following the hadith, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith is an error. It means the hadith of Fulayh, 5 and Fulayh bin Suleiman, he is not strong. 5 And his brother 5 Abdul Hamid, weaker than Falih 5"
"9332","Ali bin Hajar told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The believer’s loincloth extends to the middle of his shins, and he has no wings between it and the ankles. Whatever is lower than the ankles is in the Fire, God will not look on it. To the one who unwittingly drags his garment off.”"
"9333","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Ala bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, did you hear anything from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the garment? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The believer’s loincloth extends to the middle of his legs, with no wing on it between it and the ankles, and anything lower than that will be in the Fire, and God will not look at whoever He pulled his garment off recklessly.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9334","9416 Issa bin Hammad informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Abdul Rahman, that his father narrated to him, On the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The believer’s loincloth extends to half the shin, but it is not up to The ankles, there is no harm, and what is under the ankles is in the Fire, and God will not look at one who drags his garment out of arrogance.”"
"9335","Muhammad bin Othman Al-Uqaili informed us, saying: Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, he said: I came to Medina and came to Abu Saeed Al-Khudri and said: Did you hear from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, something about the garment? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The believer’s loincloth extends to half of his legs, with no wings between it and the ankles or below.” From that in the Fire, whoever drags his garment recklessly, God will not look at him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9336","Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, he said: Ali bin Ma’bad told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Naeem Al-Mujmar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A loincloth The believer up to the middle of his leg, not having a wing between him and the ankles, whatever is lower than the ankles will be in the Fire. He who drags his clothes on a horse. God did not look at him.”"
"9337","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’. H And Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"9338","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Isbaal in the garment, the shirt, and the turban, whoever shows any of them as a sign of arrogance, God will not look at him.” on the Day of Resurrection\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9339","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Musa bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, one of The two parts of my garment are relaxed, unless I promise to do so from him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You are not the one who does that out of arrogance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9340","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik told us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray’ told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu Qaza’ah, on the authority of Al-Asqa’ ibn Al-Ala’, on the authority of Samura, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whatever is under the ankles of the garment will be in the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9341","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, he said: Marwan used to replace Abu Hurairah. On the city, and if he saw a person dragging his garment, he would strike his foot and say: The prince has come, the prince has come, then he would say: Abu said Al-Qasim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “God does not look at one who drags his garment out of arrogance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9342","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, he said: Muslim, who is Ibn Yannaq, told us: I was sitting with Abdullah bin Omar, and he said: I heard Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, with these two ears, and he gestured with his two fingers to his ears, He says: “Whoever drags his garment without intending to wear it, meaning: anything but arrogance, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"9343","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Muslim ibn Yannaq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “Whoever drags his garment for nothing but imagination, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"9344","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muharib, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, narrating, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drags his garment out of imagination, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9345","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Jablah bin Suhaim told us, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever drags one of his clothes out of arrogance or imagination, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal combined the hadith of Muslim with Jablah."
"9346","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Jablah bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever drags one of his clothes out of imagination, God will not look at him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9347","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan Muslim bin Yannaq, he said: I saw Ibn Umar seeing a man He pulled his garment, and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever drags his garment for nothing but imagination, God will not look at him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ghandar Muhammad bin Ja`far narrated the hadith of Jabalah, and Muharib (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9348","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Muharib bin Dathar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, saying: he The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9349","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Jablah, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, saying: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And he said: “Whoever drags one of his clothes out of imagination, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9350","Amr bin Mansour informed us, saying: Al-Fadl bin Dukayn told us, on the authority of Muhammad, meaning Ibn Qais Al-Asadi, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drags his clothes out of imagination, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9351","Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Kufi and Muawiyah ibn Salih al-Dimashqi informed us, saying: Malik ibn Ismail told us, he said: Masoud ibn Saad, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, who said: “He mentioned the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: What Do they make a part of the garment at the end? He said: “They make it a hand’s length.” They said: “For it is a small span from which the private part comes out.” Muawiyah added. He said: “Then an arm’s length.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9352","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Asim bin Hilal Al-Basri told us, he said: I am Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He who drags his garment out of arrogance, God will not look at him.” Umm Salamah said: So what about us? He said: “A hand span.” She said: So what do our feet look like? He said: “Do not exceed an arm’s length.”"
"9353","Nuh ibn Habib al-Qumsi told us Bdhishi, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to me, he said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, God will not look at him.” Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of God. God, what do women do with their tails? He said: “Should it be made a span” long. I said: When their feet are uncovered? He said: “Then lengthen it by an arm and do not exceed it.”"
"9354","Mahmoud bin Khalid Al-Dimashqi told me, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Amr, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman should let her tail loosen by a span.” I said: So should it be uncovered? He said: “An cubit, do not exceed it.”"
"9355","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyd told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that she mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, women’s tails, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ Relax by a hand span.” Umm Salamah said: So should it be uncovered? He said: “Leave one arm, do not exceed it.”"
"9356","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham bin Othman Al-Basri told me, he said: Hammad, who is Ibn Masada, narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzalah, who is Ibn Abi Sufyan. He said: I heard Nafi’, saying: Umm Salamah told us that when what was mentioned about women, she said: O Messenger of God, have you seen women? He said: “A hand span.” She said: It is not enough for them. He said: “An cubit.”"
"9357","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Hanzalah, he is the son of Abi Sufyan, he said: I heard Nafi’, speaking to me, he said: He told me Some of our women, on the authority of Umm Salamah, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the Isbal that he mentioned, I said: O Messenger of God, Have you seen the women, how they are? He said: “They relax one arm.”"
"9358","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Ayoub bin Musa bin Amr bin Al-Aas told us, on the authority of Nafi’ On the authority of Safiya, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned what he mentioned about the garment, Umm Salamah said: So what about women? He said: “They are made to lengthen by a span.” She said: So do their feet appear? He said: “Then an cubit, not more than that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9359","Ammar bin Khalid Al-Wasiti Al-Tamar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiya, on the authority of Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Women’s tails are a span of span.” I said: So do their feet come out? He said: “The cubit does not increase.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9360","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: How much does a woman drag by her tail? He said: “A hand span.” She said: Then will it be uncovered? He said: “Then an cubit, do not exceed it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9361","Muhammad bin Adam Al-Masisi told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman Al-Razi, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, On the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: O Messenger of God, women’s tails? He said: “Should they be relaxed by a span.” She said: So their feet will be uncovered? He said: “One cubit, do not exceed it.” Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, that Umm Salamah mentioned Women's Tails, sent. Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, saying: Shuaib bin Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman. Ibn Ghanj, on the authority of Nafi’, that Umm Salamah mentioned women’s tails, mursal. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9362","Qutaibah told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: “The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, regarding the inclusion of a deaf woman, and that he should conceal himself in one garment, with nothing of it over his private parts.”"
"9363","Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade two kinds of clothing: covering the closed garment, and for a man to cover himself in a garment with nothing of it on his private parts.”"
"9364","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Kathir bin Hisham, he said: Ja’far bin Burqan Al-Jazari told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two types of clothing: the blind, which is for a man to wrap himself in one garment, then raise his side to his shoulders and have no other garment on him. Or a man hides himself in one garment, with nothing between him and the sky,” meaning: a covering. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9365","Harun bin Zayd bin Abi Al-Zarqa told us, he said: Abi told us, he said: Ja’far bin Burqan told us, he said: He informed me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, On the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two types of clothing: that is for a man to wrap himself in a garment over which he has no other garment, and then He raises his sides to his shoulders, or the man hides himself in one garment, with nothing between him and the sky,” meaning: a covering."
"9366","Hannad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who is Salam bin Sulaym, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad bin Umair, who said: Abu Hurairah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two types of clothing: that a man wear one garment, covering himself with it and putting his side on the his shoulders, or cover himself with one garment.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9367","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Including the deaf woman, hiding in one garment, and for the man to raise one of his legs over the other while lying on his back.”"
"9368","Muhammad bin Wahb Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told me, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim Khaled bin Abi Yazid told me, he said: Abdul Wahhab Al-Makki told me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade He greeted him with two garments. As for the two garments, a man covers himself with a garment, with nothing between him and the sky, and his remembrances reach the earth. And if he wears one garment, he takes the sides of it and places it on his shoulder, then she will be called the deaf woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9369","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Al-Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “He forbade two types of clothing: To be concealed in one garment with nothing on his private parts, or to be concealed in one garment with nothing else on him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9370","Qutaibah told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Ammar told us, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He entered the day of the conquest of Mecca, wearing a black turban, without being in ihram.”"
"9371","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Muawiyah Al-Dahni, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered on the day of the conquest, wearing a black turban.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9372","Humayd ibn Masada al-Basri told us, he said: Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “He entered The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the conquest, wearing a black turban.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9373","Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi informed us, saying: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Masawar al-Warraq, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Amr ibn Harith ibn Umayyah, On the authority of his father, he said: “It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the pulpit, wearing a black turban. He placed it between his shoulders.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9374","Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Masawar al-Warraq, on the authority of Ja`far bin Amr bin Harith, on the authority of his father, said: “I saw on the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a burning turban.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9375","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: We told him 5 Ibn Nufayl Abu Ja`far al-Nufaili al-Harrani is trustworthy 5, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, he said : Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amr told me, on the authority of Busr ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Makhramah ibn Sulayman, he said: I and some of my companions entered upon Zayd. Ibn Khalid Al-Juhani, so we sat down, and behold, in his house there were two signs and a curtain with pictures on it, so we said to him: Didn’t you tell us that the angels do not Do you enter a house in which there is a picture? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Except a number on a garment, or a garment that has a number on it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9376","Safwan bin Amr Al-Homsi told us, he said: Abdul-Wahhab bin Najda told us, he said: Abdul-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubaida bin Sufyan, who said: I and Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman entered upon We went back to Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani, and we found with him two tablets with pictures on them. Abu Salamah said: Didn’t you tell us that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Angels do not enter a house in which there is an image.” Zaid said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Except a number in \Gown\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9377","Issa bin Hammad bin Zaghbah told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj told me, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid al-Juhani, on the authority of Abu Talha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Angels do not enter a house in which A picture.” Busr said: Then Zaid complained, so we went back to him, and behold, on his door was a curtain with a picture on it, so I said to Ubayd Allah Al-Khawlani: Didn’t he tell us? More than the picture on the first day? He said: Ubayd Allah said: Didn’t you hear him say: “Except a number on a garment?”"
"9378","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir bin Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yasar Abi Al-Hubab, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, on the authority of Abu Talha, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog, or statue"
"9379","Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told me, he said: Ibn Ishaq told me, on the authority of Salim Abi Al-Nadr, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, he said: Uthman bin Hunaif and I went out to go back to Abu Talha in a complaint, so we entered upon it and under it was a wall with pictures in it. He said: Remove this from Under me, then Othman said to him: If you had not heard, O Abu Talha, Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he forbade pictures, he said: “Except a number in A garment, or a garment with a number on it?” He said: “Yes, but it would be better for me to remove it from under me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9380","Ali bin Shuaib Al-Baghdadi told us, he said: Maan bin Issa Al-Fazzar Abu Yahya told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Nadr, On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, he went to see Abu Talha al-Ansari to visit him, and he found Sahl ibn Hanif with him, so Abu Talha ordered A person was removing a pattern underneath, and Sahl said to him: Why did you remove it? He said: Because it contains pictures, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about them what you have learned. He said: Didn’t he say: “Except what is a pattern on a garment?” He said: Yes, but it is better for me."
"9381","Muhammad bin Hashim Al-Baalbaki told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, He said: Abu Talha told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9382","Yazid bin Muhammad bin Abdul Samad told us, he said: Hisham bin Ismail told us, he said: Hqal told us, and he is Ibn Ziyad, he said: Al-Awza’i told us. On the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah told me that he heard Ibn Abbas, saying: I heard Abu Talha, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9383","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. H Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Talha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9384","Wahb bin Bayan told me, he said: Ibn Wahb told me, he said: Yunus told me, Ibn Shihab said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah told me, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he heard him say: I heard Abu Talha saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Angels do not enter A house in which there is a dog, and no pictures.”"
"9385","Muhammad bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Al-Shawareb told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Talha, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog. Nor the image of graven images.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9386","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, that Bukayr told him, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the house, he found in it a picture of Abraham and a picture of Mary, so he said: “As for them, They have heard that angels do not enter a house in which there is an image, and this is Abraham with an image, so why is it upright?”"
"9387","Masoud bin Juwayriyah Al-Mawsili told us, he said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ali, he said I prepared food, so I called the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came and entered and saw a curtain with pictures on it, so he came out and said: “The angels do not enter.” A verse in which there are images.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9388","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri told us, he is Muhammad bin Abdullah, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Urwa On the authority of Aisha, there was a decorated curtain over her door, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Aisha, delay this, for I When I see him, I remember the world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9389","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, he said: told us Ezra, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: It was We have a curtain in which is a statue of a bird facing the house when someone enters. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Aisha, turn it around. Every time I entered and saw him, I was reminded of the world.” She said: “And we had a piece of velvet with a flag on it, so we used to wear it, but we did not cut it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9390","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr told us, he said: Bukayr told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin told me. Al-Qasim said that his father told him, on the authority of Aisha, that she had put up a curtain with pictures on it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and removed it. So she cut him two pillows, and a man in the gathering at that time, called Rabi’ah bin Ata, said: I heard Abu Muhammad, meaning Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was kind to them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9391","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, he said: I heard al-Qasim He narrates, on the authority of Aisha, who said: There was a garment in my house with pictures on it, so I put it on while I was away in the house, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, prayed to him, then he said: “O Aisha, take it away from me.” So she took it off and made it a cushion. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9392","Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Qutayba bin Saeed told us, and the wording is for Ishaq. He said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad narrates on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me, and I covered myself. In a grave in which there were statues, and when he saw them, his face changed, then he mauled them with his own hand, and said: “The people who will be most severely tormented on the Day of Resurrection are those who resemble By God’s creation.” Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, and she said: We cut it up and made one or two pillows out of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9393","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He presented The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came from a journey, and I had inadvertently covered myself with a cover of mine in which there were statues. He took it off and said: “The most severe of people will be tormented on the Day of Resurrection, those who match God’s creation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9394","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left and then entered, and I had hung a pen in which were horses with wings. She said: When he saw him, he said: \Take it off\"""""""
"9395","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Khalid, who is Ibn Al-Harith, told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, He said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas, when a man from the people of Iraq came to him and said: I am making these pictures, so what do you say about them? He said: Bring it closer, bring it closer. I heard Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever makes a picture in this world, will be required on the Day of Resurrection to blow it.” In it is the spirit, and there is no one who can breathe it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9396","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever creates a picture, God will punish him until he breathes the soul into it, and he is not the one who breathed into it.”"
"9397","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever creates an image will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the soul into it, and he will not be a blower.”"
"9398","Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Ibrahim bin Ishkab told us, on the authority of Qarad, who is Abd al-Rahman bin Ghazwan. He said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Aoun, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God Almighty tortures photographers.” for what they depicted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9399","Muhammad bin Khalil al-Dimashqi told us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah told him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, those who make images on the Day of Resurrection will be told: Bring to life what you created.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9400","Qutaibah told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayoub. And Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Thaqafi told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “The people who make these images will be tortured on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Bring to life what you have created.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9401","Masoud bin Juwayriyah told us, he said: Al-Mu’afa told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “Those who make images will be brought, and it will be said to them: Bring to life what you have created.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9402","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The makers of these pictures will be tortured on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Bring to life what you created.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9403","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Sammak, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, she said: “The people who will be most severely tormented on the Day of Resurrection are those who are equal to God in His creation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9404","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Imran bin Hattan, that Aisha I told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “did not leave anything in his house that had a cross on it, unless he tore it off.”"
"9405","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Dafra, Umm Abd al-Rahman bin Udhaynah, told me, She said: We were walking around with the Mother of the Believers, Aisha, and she saw on a woman a garment with sclerosis on it, so she said: Throw it away, for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: “If he sees something like this, he will punish him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
